nwhere ${Σ}_{r}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of ${Σ}_{r}.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\n{Σ}_{r}^{+}=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{U}_{r}^{T}=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & ={V}_{r}\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}\\,{U}_{r}^{T} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e061f4a4-b39c-59c9-9f05-767e4bc6ebb4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420794}}] :activity/title "Singular Value Decomposition and the Pseudoinverse Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420758}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444702} :activity/id #uuid "30659c6c-04d6-5d4c-8a94-17b535625cad" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049503 :topic/id #uuid "fa18866e-f310-5b54-8bcb-21e9073c9cde" :topic/math-academy-id 3134} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444699 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d12f43f6-0163-5178-9184-8181315772e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371799} {:answer/id #uuid "66741388-c98e-51a6-8c1f-3e8c2fd9f23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371800} {:answer/id #uuid "6e